# Build-time settings. Copy this file to .env.local and fill it in.
#
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# .env.local is gitignored (covered by *.local), which is the point: neither
# value belongs in the repo. A shell variable of the same name still overrides
# what is here, so CI and the Cloudflare dashboard, which set the shell
# variable, are unaffected.
#
# All four are optional. Left unset, SITE_ORIGIN defaults to the production
# domain, the privacy page keeps its CONTACT-EMAIL-PLACEHOLDER (with the build
# warning every run until a real address is supplied), no analytics beacon is
# injected at all, and no forum link is drawn anywhere.

# The controller contact address printed on the published privacy policy. It
# has to be a mailbox someone actually reads: the build refuses an address that
# looks like an example. A dedicated forwarding alias beats a personal inbox,
# since it sits on a public page and is where a data-protection request lands.
CONTACT_EMAIL=

# The canonical origin. Baked into every lesson page as its canonical link,
# hreflang alternates and Open Graph tags, and into the app shell's own social
# preview, so whatever host it names is the one that circulates. Only change it
# for a fork or a different domain; the default is correct for production.
# SITE_ORIGIN=https://confoundle.org

# Cloudflare Web Analytics site token, from the Cloudflare dashboard under
# Web Analytics, for the confoundle.org site. Unset means no beacon is injected,
# which is the right default for a fork: nobody else's traffic should land in
# this project's dashboard. What it does and does not collect is published in
# the "How visits are counted" section of public/privacy.html, and that section
# has to stay true to whatever is configured here.
CF_ANALYTICS_TOKEN=

# The discussion forum's ORIGIN, and nothing else: scheme and host, no path, no
# query, no trailing anything. A value carrying a path is rejected and the link
# disappears rather than pointing somewhere wrong, because the URL most likely
# to be pasted here is the one the forum owner has open, which is /admin.
#
# Unset means the feature does not exist: no link is drawn on any card. That is
# the correct default for a fork, and it is also correct until the forum is
# ready, since a "Discuss" link into an empty forum is worse than none.
#
# BEFORE SETTING THIS, change one Discourse setting. The link points at a TAG
# page, one tag per card, named with the card's own slug. Discourse by default
# only lets staff create tags, so on a fresh forum the first reader to open a
# thread cannot apply the tag and the scheme never bootstraps. Set the minimum
# trust level to create tags low enough that ordinary members can, or pre-create
# the tags. See docs/forum.md.
# VITE_FORUM_ORIGIN=https://confoundle.discourse.group
